{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Border of the north.</b> The northern boundary." "<b>From the Great Sea you shall mark out for yourselves Mount Hor.</b> For it is at the northwest corner, and its peak slopes out and extends into the sea — and there is the width of the sea inland from it and seaward from it." "<b>You shall mark out.</b> You shall slope for yourselves — to turn from west to north, toward Mount Hor." "<b>You shall mark out.</b> A term of extension, as in ״אֶל תָּא הָרָצִים״ (I Kings 14), ״וְתָאֵי הַשַּׁעַר״ (Ezekiel 40) — the vestibule, which they call אפנדי\"ץ, which is set at an angle and slopes."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:44.785730137Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}